  },
  "articleBody": "When you're getting quotes for interior trim painting, asking the right questions can make all the difference in avoiding surprises and ensuring you get the results you want. Here's a handy checklist of things to cover:\n\n1.  **What's included in the scope?** Make sure to clarify if baseboards, door casings, window trim, crown molding, and closet trim are all covered. Also, will adjacent walls be protected or repainted?\n2.  **What's the prep process?** Ask about sanding, caulking, and whether priming will be done. This is crucial for a lasting finish.\n3.  **What paint product and finish will be used?** Knowing the specific paint line and sheen helps you understand the quality and durability.\n4.  **How will repairs be handled?** If there are dents or gaps, understand if repairs are included in the quote and to what extent.\n5.  **What's the timeline?** Ask how soon they can start and how many days the project is expected to take.\n6.  **What about old homes?** If your home is older, bring up any concerns about lead paint abatement and how they address it.\n7.  **How is cleanup handled?** Clarify expectations for furniture moving, protection of belongings, and post-job cleanup.\n\nGetting these details ironed out upfront with a professional like HH Remodeling LLC ensures everyone is on the same page and helps you achieve beautiful, long-lasting results for your trim.",
